{"id": "EUVD-2014-9827", "enisaUuid": "8ca1e6b4-b686-3d63-bbe4-0e5217763dbe", "description": "ChurcHope theme for WordPress before 2.2 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to download arbitrary files through the 'file' parameter of /wp-content/themes/churchope/lib/downloadlink.php. Attackers can supply directory traversal sequences to read sensitive files like wp-config.php or /etc/passwd, exposing database credentials. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-18.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T02:07:38", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/3c5833bd-1fe0-4eba-97aa-7d3a0c8fda15", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/129706/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/churchope-lfi.yaml", "https://web.archive.org/web/20220629224817/https://www.cloudways.com/en/best-wordpress-themes/nonprofit/church", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/churchope-wordpress-theme-2.2-path-traversal-via-downloadlink-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2014-125134", "GHSA-949v-g35q-94ph"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7ae92887-44bb-345c-b62a-7bbaf9476bb2", "product": {"name": "ChurcHope", "vendor": {"name": "ChurcHope"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7ab8091f-b40b-3122-af3e-d572250141e1", "vendor": {"name": "ChurcHope"}}], "isExploited": false}